WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.736
-So, this is a great documentary
about sort of the '90s

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:04.970
and Bad Boy Records.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.805
But it also --
kind of what brings it together

00:00:06.805 --> 00:00:09.241
is you had a 20th reunion
concert with everybody.

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:10.643
-Yes. Yes.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.945
-Was that nerve-racking?
Was that exciting?

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:15.215
How did you feel in the time
leading up to that concert?

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:17.616
Because that was --
We saw you sort of talking about

00:00:17.616 --> 00:00:19.786
the lights you wanted
with your staff.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:20.854
-Yeah. It was --

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:21.887
-Did you get the lights
you wanted?

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:22.922
Did you get the God light?

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.057
-Yeah. Yeah.
I got the God light.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.492
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:27.994
But it really was
like a family reunion,

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:31.464
when you don't know what's going
to happen at a family reunion,

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.400
and there's some unresolved
issues with a lot of the family.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.834
-Yeah.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:38.504
-So we started it out as like,
just a concert documentary,

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:40.039
but when we got together,

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:43.676
we had to deal with the issues
about career and our lives

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:47.080
and things that we haven't
dealt with together.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.348
And it really -- just really
showed the story of

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:53.686
our evolution, and our ups and
downs, trials and tribulations,

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:56.656
life, death, and overall
at the end of the day,

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:59.191
victory for us all
being together

00:00:59.191 --> 00:01:00.526
on one stage at one time.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.195
-It was really wonderful.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.996
You talk about life and death,

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:06.432
which is of course one of the
parts of this story.

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:09.469
Biggie kind of hangs over
the story of Bad Boy Records.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:12.505
-Yes.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.307
-It seems like that's something
you reflect on every day.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.742
-Yes.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.278
-Was it helpful to reflect on it
with everybody from that era?

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:23.316
-Yeah, it was definitely helpful
to reflect on it with everybody

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:27.487
that was in the Bad Boy family
and on the label

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:30.523
because we all were traumatized
by it.

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.358
But it wasn't just us.
It was our fans,

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.060
and it was
the people of Brooklyn.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.597
So us all being able to come
back together on his birthday

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:40.366
and have this concert,
it kind of gave us some closure

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.402
and we were able to kind of
put it behind us

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:44.671
and celebrate his life.

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.806
-It was really great.
You did two nights.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.007
You felt better about
the second night.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.008
-Yes, yes.

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.342
-Was this just sort of athletes

00:01:50.342 --> 00:01:52.846
who maybe needed to get back
into the groove?

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.013
Is that what you felt like?

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.281
-Yeah, I mean,
I'm a perfectionist,

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.982
and most people that came to
the first show,

00:01:56.982 --> 00:01:58.384
they really loved
the first show,

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:00.586
but I knew that the things
that went wrong,

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.955
and that's always been the thing
about me,

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.124
is that I'm very, very hard
on myself,

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:08.160
and the first show was like --

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.330
The next morning I was crying,
and my kids --

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.133
I told my kids I needed to come
up to the hotel room

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:16.802
because I just needed somebody
to cry in front of

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:18.037
because I was so disappointed.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.773
I was like a kid
in Little League.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.074
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:23.609
So I'm kind of, like, spoiled
with the performances --

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:24.811
-Wait. You called your children

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.179
because you wanted to cry
in front of them?

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.480
-Yeah. I mean --

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.415
-That seems like it would be
very traumatic for them.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.883
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:34.187
But I was crying alone,
and I felt lonely --

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:36.455
-Yeah, there we go.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:37.723
-I needed somebody to tell me
it was going to be all right.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.526
-You do plenty for them.
You do plenty for them.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:40.626
-Exactly.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:41.660
-It's about time they do
something for you.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.029
-It was the first time
they saw it,

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:45.732
and I just, you know,
I was in a desperate situation,

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.333
and I called my family --
-There you go.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.735
-And I was like,
"I'm up here crying.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:49.902
Y'all need to get up here."

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:51.404
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:54.240
But the second night --
The second night really --

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.075
I mean, you really got to go
see the movie.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.478
"Can't Stop Won't Stop."

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.979
It's in theaters
just up till this week.

00:03:00.979 --> 00:03:03.649
We did a limited run,
but you can go to Apple Music,

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:05.318
and you can get it there.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:07.554
And it will also be on iTunes
July 7th.

